    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Energy conversion</span> is the changing of energy from one form to another. Energy is never created or destroyed — this is the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">principle of conservation of energy</span> — only transformed, and in every real conversion some energy is lost as heat.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Principle of Conservation of Energy</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">The total energy in an isolated system remains constant. When energy changes form, the total amount before and after the change is the same, although useful energy output is always less than input because of losses such as friction and heat.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Common Energy Conversions</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Device</th><th>Energy conversion</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Electric iron / heater</td><td>Electrical → heat (thermal)</td></tr><tr><td>Generator / dynamo</td><td>Mechanical → electrical</td></tr><tr><td>Electric motor</td><td>Electrical → mechanical</td></tr><tr><td>Solar panel</td><td>Light (solar) → electrical</td></tr><tr><td>Battery (discharging)</td><td>Chemical → electrical</td></tr><tr><td>Battery (charging)</td><td>Electrical → chemical</td></tr><tr><td>Loudspeaker</td><td>Electrical → sound</td></tr><tr><td>Microphone</td><td>Sound → electrical</td></tr><tr><td>Bulb (filament)</td><td>Electrical → light and heat</td></tr><tr><td>Car engine</td><td>Chemical (fuel) → heat → mechanical</td></tr><tr><td>Photosynthesis</td><td>Light → chemical energy</td></tr><tr><td>Falling body</td><td>Potential → kinetic</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Efficiency of Energy Conversion</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Efficiency = (useful energy output ÷ total energy input) × 100%. No machine is 100% efficient because some input energy is always converted to heat through friction or resistance.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> When asked for the energy conversion in a device, state it as 'X energy to Y energy', in the correct order, e.g. 'electrical energy to mechanical energy' for a motor, not the reverse.</div>",
